in London British authorities are being  asked some tough questions this morning  as they piece together the chain of  events that led to two people being  killed and three others injured in a  terror attack near London Bridge on  Friday the suspect was a convicted  terrorist he had been deemed a threat to  the public in the past he was shot and  killed by police the attack was in the  same place of another terror incident  two years ago Holly Williams has the  latest from London this morning Holly  good morning good morning well the  attacker was named this morning as Osman  Khan a convicted terrorist who was  jailed in 2012 for plotting to blow up  the London Stock Exchange he was  released early and he was on probation  the British media is reporting he'd  agreed to wear an electronic monitor he  was apparently a lone attacker armed  with a knife and a determination to kill  in this exclusive video from the Daily  Mail bystanders are seen fighting him  back with fire extinguishers they  tackled him to the ground  an act of breathtaking heroism according  to London's mayor a plainclothes police  officer removed his weapon and the  police shot him at close range he was  wearing what the police are calling a  hoax suicide vest Thomas grey says he  was one of those who stepped in he was  you know wielding two knives one was  sort of duct-taped to his hand so all I  could do what what after the guys had  sort of held him down and was sort of  pinning into the ground you know kind of  trying to stamp his how did I put on his  restaurant you know release the knife  Richard Walton is the former head of  counterterrorism for the London Police  in the last 18 months to two years  they've been 22 disrupted terrorist  plots in the UK that's a high number of  attacks plots that have been disrupted  and this is the first attack in the UK  since 2017 but the terrible irony is  that Khan reportedly set off on his  stabbing spree while attending a  conference on rehabilitating prisoners  many here are asking why he was released  from jail early  including the British prime minister I  have long argued that it is a mistake to  allow serious and violent criminals to  come out of prison early a house outside  of London was searched overnight in  connection with this attack Dana Polly  thank you very much
 

